{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in specifications. The policy gives forward motion in clear conditions, uses short directed turns for side/front obstacles, allows a rare one-shot backward escape only from a dedicated front-obstacle recovery path, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure state. Action states are one-shot and obstacle events can preempt them for safety, while path_clear usually self-loops in action states to preserve the intended pulse in the same step.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in G",
    "Use one policy specification with perception and one-shot action states to enforce safe progress-oriented behavior",
    "Add a small specification to make full_rotate reachable only after repeated front-blocked recovery failure"
  ],
